      },
      "text": "Wet processing is the most chemistry-intensive part of textile manufacturing and the largest source of wastewater pollution. The ~200 kilometers of rivers around industrial textile districts in China, Bangladesh, and India are often so heavily contaminated that satellite imagery shows dye releases."
